      "data": {
        "title": "Draft #2: Write down what a canon template is",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-templates-in-order",
          "nodeId": "canon-templates-in-order-task-draft-2"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "body": "The standard each keeper is rebuilt to: Glyph, Summary and Detail (no Icon unless it earns one); views derived by the template's own Method; the graph window in the Detail's shape; relationships in the shared edge vocabulary; its classes and Method handed on through one export. The Task Template already works this way. Proposed as wording first, and written into canon only after approval.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792449096026,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "startedAt": "2026-10-21T00:30:48.090Z",
        "completedAt": "2026-10-21T04:04:59.077Z",
        "notes": "The wording was approved by Michael and written into canon as library/templates/root.node. The mechanical rules are an audit (tests/helpers/templateStandard.js) that tests/canonTemplates.test.js runs over every canon template: new ones must meet it, and the Page Template family is on a known list until it is rebuilt."
      }
    },
