    {
      "id": "canon-templates-in-order-list-canon",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "1. Become canon templates (7)",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 1240
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 560,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-templates-in-order",
          "nodeId": "canon-templates-in-order-list-canon"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## 1. Become canon templates (7)\n\nRebuilt to the standard (Glyph, Summary and Detail; views derived by the template's own Method; window in the Detail's shape; one export). Approved in principle; collection and workboard moved to group 4, and the plan template stays its own template and is **not** merged into the Task Template.\n\n| Template | What it is | Used by | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `idea-template` | Frame, test and advance an idea (21 classes) | 59 | The anchor of the thinking family; by far the most used. |\n| `topic-template` | Understand a complex subject: concepts, claims, mechanisms, sources | 11 | Thinking family. |\n| `question-driven-explanation-template` | Explain a subject through questions and direct answers | 9 | Thinking family. |\n| `plan-template` | Goals, phases, actions, milestones, decisions, constraints, risks, contingencies | 14 | Its own template. Not folded into the Task Template. |\n| `public-arrival-template` | A front door for a public graph | 5 | Four classes. |\n| `edge-class-template` | How an edge class is authored (11 classes) | 12 | Canon's own edge classes, including the six task ones, were cloned from it. |\n| `node-class-template` | How a node class is authored | 2 | The task classes were authored by hand; this is how they should be. |\n"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "canon-templates-in-order-list-fold",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "2. Fold into another, or retire (2)",
      "position": {
        "x": 1600,
        "y": 1240
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 340,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-templates-in-order",
          "nodeId": "canon-templates-in-order-list-fold"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## 2. Fold into another, or retire (2)\n\nNot rebuilt on their own.\n\n| Template | What it is | Used by | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `brainstorm-template` | A loose staging ground for ideas, questions and constraints before promotion | 1 | Fold into the idea template. |\n| `task-template-demo` | The demo the Task Template was built from | 0 | Retire: canon has the Task Template. |\n"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "canon-templates-in-order-list-primitives",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "3. Superseded by a primitives page already in canon (11) — approved",
      "position": {
        "x": 2560,
        "y": 1240
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 760,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-templates-in-order",
          "nodeId": "canon-templates-in-order-list-primitives"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## 3. Superseded by a primitives page already in canon (11) — approved\n\n**Approved:** canon already has a page for each of these primitives, so the starters are not rebuilt. They stay in your library as reference.\n\n| Template | What it is | Used by | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `content-template` | Where a node's real material lives | 2 | Canon: primitives/content. |\n| `glyph-template` | The single port a Surface's chain ends on | 2 | Canon: primitives/glyph. |\n| `membrane-template` | Three chained Membrane nodes making a custom boundary | 0 | Canon: primitives/membrane. |\n| `method-template` | An event-raising Method wired to a second Method | 1 | Canon: primitives/method. |\n| `port-template` | The interface socket a Declaration exposes | 2 | Canon: primitives/port. |\n| `portal-template` | A real, resolvable jump to another graph | 1 | Canon: primitives/portal. |\n| `property-template` | A property node and its Method | 0 | Canon: primitives/property. |\n| `view-template` | Where a View authors its own interface | 3 | Canon: primitives/face. |\n| `node-template` | The minimal reference for how a node wires its presentation | 0 | Canon: primitives/surface. |\n| `declaration-template` | What a new graph looks like: a page walking through a Declaration | 5 | Canon: primitives/root. |\n| `stroke-control` | One edge paint layer, authored as Properties | 0 | Canon: edges/classes/stroke. |\n"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "canon-templates-in-order-list-call",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "4. Redo from scratch, or your call (6)",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 1940
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 620,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-templates-in-order",
          "nodeId": "canon-templates-in-order-list-call"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## 4. Redo from scratch, or your call (6)\n\nCollection and workboard: what exists will not suffice, so converting it is the wrong job. Either we redo them from scratch (a design first), or we drop them. Do we need them?\n\n| Template | What it is | Used by | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `collection-template` | A directory-backed collection with a bounded window of members | 16 | Redo from scratch, or drop. Used by 16 graphs today. |\n| `collection-window-controller` | Discovers and projects a window of collection members | 13 | Goes with the collection. |\n| `workboard-template` | An operational workboard backed by task graphs | 9 | Redo from scratch, or drop. The Task Template now shows status itself. |\n| `handle-template` | A custom decoration drawn on a specific port | 0 | No canon primitive yet. I would make one, with a template, alongside the custom handles work. |\n| `wikipedia-article-template` | A graph-backed Wikipedia article node with semantic views | 6 | Canon template, canon example, or leave in your library? |\n| `smoke-test-template` | A quiet environment for focused smoke tests | 1 | I would leave it in your library. |\n"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
