        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-templates-in-order",
          "nodeId": "canon-templates-in-order-list-remove"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## 5. Approved for removal — after the repo template (2)\n\n**Approved:** neither is a template (no root graph in the folder), and both can go. **Not yet:** nothing is thrown away from your library until the repo template is done, because it decides how the library is laid out. The clean-out is its own task, after the repo template.\n\n| Template | What it is | Used by | What the clean-out does |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `lionel` | A set of edge and node classes for a project of its own | 4 | Deletes the folder. The four graphs in people/ that use its classes (alex-jones, laura-loomer, robert-barnes, roger-stone) lose their class bindings and stay as unrendered reference. |\n| `bridge-template` | Two example graphs (an export and an import) | 1 | Deletes the folder. The Bridge primitives page replaces it; the primitive-template-collection task and the canon-or-personal census that mention it are left as they are. |\n"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
