        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## Where canon stands against it\n\nThe mechanical rules, run over every template now in canon (the audit is `tests/helpers/templateStandard.js`):\n\n| Template | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `task-template` | Meets every rule. |\n| `page-template` | Out of standard on rules 1 (it still has an Icon view), 2 (its views are out of shape) and 6 (its window is not 3:2). It meets 3, 8, 9 and 10 and is valid. |\n| the eight Page Template demos | The same three, because they are copies; the poster also fails 7 (three edges are drawn by side), and the slides demo also fails 5 (a scrolling area inside a card). They are regenerated from the template, not edited. |\n\nThe other six templates that become canon are not in canon yet: each will be rebuilt to the standard before it goes in, and the audit will check it.\n"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
