    {
      "id": "canon-templates-in-order-list-audit",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "6. The audit, 30 October 2026",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 2740
      },
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 1300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-templates-in-order",
          "nodeId": "canon-templates-in-order-list-audit"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## 6. The audit, 30 October 2026\n\nRead-only. Every template and class graph in canon, the personal library and the app's public folder (449 graphs) was loaded, run through the validator and the retired-vocabulary check, and, for templates, the canon template standard (`tests/helpers/templateStandard.js`). Nothing was changed by the audit.\n\n### Canon: finished\n\nAll fourteen templates in canon meet the standard (`tests/canonTemplates.test.js`, known list empty): the Page Template and its eight demos, the Task, Collection, Repo and Declaration templates, and the Starter. The Declaration Template is in canon now, so it is no longer left over; the personal one is superseded by the Root primitive page.\n\n### The seven that are to be rebuilt\n\nAll seven are valid and use current words. What they lack is the standard itself: Glyph, Summary and Detail views derived by their own Method, a window in the Detail's shape, one export, an environment, and canon addresses (rule numbers from the standard).\n\n| Template | Used by | Fails rules | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `idea-template` | 54 files | 1, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9, 13 | Anchor of the thinking family. Brainstorm folds into it. 21 classes (11 node, 10 edge). |\n| `topic-template` | 19 | 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9, 13 | 7 classes. |\n| `question-driven-explanation-template` | 14 | 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9, 13 | 7 classes. |\n| `plan-template` | 23 | 1, 2, 3, 6, 8, 9, 13 | 9 classes. Its own template. |\n| `public-arrival-template` | 10 | 1, 2, 3, 6, 8, 9, 13 | 4 classes. |\n| `edge-class-template` | 25 | 1, 2, 6, 7, 8, 9, 13 | Already has a Method that derives. 11 classes, none of them used by anything else. |\n| `node-class-template` | 6 | 1, 2, 6, 8, 9, 13 | Already has a Method that derives. 3 classes. |\n\n### Reference only: nothing to do (superseded by a primitives page)\n\n`content`, `glyph`, `membrane`, `method`, `port`, `portal`, `property`, `view`, `node`, `declaration` and `declaration-template-trial` (a second copy of the Declaration Template). All valid except: **`stroke-control` has 10 validation errors**. None is rebuilt. The trial copy can go at the clean-out.\n\n### Broken, and going nowhere\n\n| Graph | Problem | Says |\n|---|---|---|\n| `collection-template` | 1 error, 4 warnings, 4 retired words | Canon has a Collection template that replaces it. Used by 24 files, all of which would be reference. |\n| `collection-window-controller` | 1 error | Goes with the old collection. |\n| `workboard-template` | 1 error | The Task Template shows status itself. |\n| `stroke-control` | 10 errors | Canon has the stroke class. |\n\nI would retire these four (leave the files, unlisted) rather than rebuild them.\n\n### Your call\n\n- `handle-template`: valid, a stub (7 nodes), used by one file. Still waiting on making the handle a canon primitive.\n- `wikipedia-article-template`: valid, 16 nodes, 6 files. Canon template, canon example, or yours?\n- `smoke-test-template`: valid, used by one file. I would leave it where it is.\n- `task-template-demo`: used by nothing; canon has the Task Template. Retire.\n- `brainstorm-template`: folds into idea.\n\n### The node class library (the case that showed the size)\n\n- 13 old packages under `library/classes/nodes/` (agent-prompting, data-schema, document-publishing, knowledge-research, narrative-story, onboarding, product-project, skill-contract, spatial-environment, template-structure, type-definition, ui-interaction, workflow-execution): **108 classes, 102 use retired vocabulary and 100 fail validation.**\n- The app's own `public/library/classes/nodes/` holds a second copy of them (75 of the files are byte-for-byte the same as canon's).\n- What is current there: the task-planning package (10 of 15 are node classes in the new form), the Collection and Repo classes, and every class that belongs to a template (Page Template and its demos, 5 each).\n- Where the old packages are named from outside, it is by the template gallery, the `agent` and `graph-theory` pages, archived tutorials and old contracts. I did not check each reference one by one: a filename match is not proof that a class is in use.\n\n### The order\n\n1. **Decide** (yours): the four retirements above, `wikipedia`, `handle`, and what to do with the old class packages (retire as a group, or choose which to keep).\n2. **Clean-out**, as approved: `lionel`, `bridge-template`, then whatever step 1 retires. A list first.\n3. **Rebuild the seven**, in order of use: idea (with brainstorm), topic, question-driven explanation, plan, public arrival, then edge-class and node-class. The three thinking templates share their way of working, so they go together.\n4. **Node classes** (task `p6`): rebuild only the classes a rebuilt template or a kept graph needs, and leave the rest unrendered.\n5. Then the tutorial pass."
        }
      }
    }
